# PTO provenance network: the HR absence-management chain of registries/industry/intranet_agents_with_tools.hocon
# (MyIntranet -> HR -> AbsenceManagement -> ScheduleLeaveAPI), kept with the same instructions, trimmed to that chain.
#
# Changes from the original:
#   - Other departments, CheckLeaveBalancesAPI and URLProvider are removed (so the URL instructions are removed too).
#   - ScheduleLeaveAPI runs task_verification/pto_provenance/coded_tools/schedule_pto.py, which writes to a spoof SQLite
#     HR database, and takes employee_id as an argument (prototype: a real deployment would take the employee from
#     the signed-in user, not from the agent).
#   - ProvenanceMiddleware on AbsenceManagement records every ScheduleLeaveAPI call in the provenance graph and verifies
#     it against the database. The agent never sees the verdict.
#   - Claude Haiku 4.5, and step and time limits (the original has none).

{
    include "registries/aaosa.hocon",
    include "registries/expertise_scoping_instructions.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Research pilot: intranet HR chain that schedules PTO in a spoof database, with every tool call recorded and verified in a provenance graph.",
        "tags": ["experimental", "task_verification"],
        "sample_queries": ["I'm employee E-1042. Please schedule PTO for me on December 3, 2026."]
    },

    "llm_config": {
        "class": "langchain_anthropic.chat_models.ChatAnthropic",
        "model_name": "claude-haiku-4-5"
    },
    "max_steps": 40,
    "max_execution_seconds": 300,

    "instructions_prefix": """
    You are in charge of a portion of company's intranet. The intranet is also known as MyIntranet.
    Always ask your down-chain agents for their take on the inquiry, and delegate to them as much as possible
    to fulfill the user's inquiry.
    If needed ask the user for clarification.
    """ ${expertise_scoping_instructions},

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "MyIntranet",
            "function": {
                "description": """
                Your name is MyIntranet. You respond to employee inquiries related to company's intranet.
                Your down-chain agents (or tools) will help you determine your scope of operations.
                """
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "query": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "An employee inquiry about company intranet resources, HR policies or other corporate services."
                        },
                    },
                    "required": ["query"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
You are the top-level agent responsible for handling all inquiries to company's intranet chatbot.
When interacting with the user, act as the single point of interaction. No need to mention the other tools or agents.
Do as much as you can to answer the inquiry, relying on your down-chain agents as needed.
If there are any requirements that need user input, ask them one at a time, with clear examples of the choices available.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["HR"]
        },
        {
            "name": "HR",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles HR-related inquiries including employee benefits, payroll, immigration, absence management, vacation, PTO, recruitment, onboarding, and workplace policies."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
You are responsible for HR-related inquiries for company's employees.
That includes payroll, benefits, immigration questions, as well as and absence management:
vacation, PTO, other time-off and checking leave balances.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["AbsenceManagement"]
        },
        {
            "name": "AbsenceManagement",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles absence management tasks including vacation requests, PTO balances, sick leave, time-off scheduling, and leave balance inquiries."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
You handle absence management-related tasks for company's employees (i.e., vacation, PTO, or other time-off).
Always return a concrete answer from your tools.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "middleware": [
                {
                    "class": "task_verification.pto_provenance.provenance_middleware.ProvenanceMiddleware",
                    "args": {"tools": ["ScheduleLeaveAPI"]}
                }
            ],
            "tools": ["ScheduleLeaveAPI"]
        },
        {
            "name": "ScheduleLeaveAPI",
            "function": {
                "description": """
Directly schedules a leave for a specific start date and end date for company's employees.
For a single day, end date can be automatically set to start date.
Return what the tool returns, formatted in markdown.
                """,
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "employee_id": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The employee ID of the person taking the leave, e.g. E-1042"
                        },
                        "start_date": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The start date of the leave, YYYY-MM-DD"
                        },
                        "end_date": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The end date of the leave, YYYY-MM-DD"
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["employee_id", "start_date", "end_date"]
                }
            },
            "class": "task_verification.pto_provenance.coded_tools.schedule_pto.SchedulePto"
        }
    ]
}
